code: 0
--- stdout
Process from .github/dojo.toml: board acme/12, issues in acme/payments.
Find an issue to take with gh dojo next (Backlog or no status, no unresolved blockers);
read it with gh dojo show <N>.
Run a verb as gh dojo <verb> <N>; --dry-run shows its plan first.
Every command takes --json (schema_version 1), --jq and --template, as gh does.

Verbs:
  start           You begin writing the change
                  optional --comment; refused while a blocker is unresolved; assigns you; comments "Started. Session: {session} {comment}"
  hold            Work is stuck: waiting for another issue or an outside decision
                  needs --by or --comment; labels +blocked; --by N also marks it blocked by #N; comments "On hold until {by}. {comment}"
  resume          What held the issue is resolved
                  optional --comment; refused while a blocker is unresolved; labels -blocked; comments "{comment}"
  review          The pull request is open and ready for review
                  needs --comment and --assignee; refused with the label blocked; refused while a blocker is unresolved; labels +needs-review -changes-requested; assigns the --assignee user; comments "Ready for review by @{assignee}: {comment}"
  request-changes The reviewer asked for changes; the author makes them and runs review again
                  needs --comment; labels +changes-requested -needs-review; assigns you; unassigns everyone else; comments "Changes requested: {comment}"
  approve         The user approved the pull request after reviewing it
                  optional --comment; the user's decision: ask first, then --yes; refused with the label blocked; labels -needs-review; assigns you; unassigns everyone else; comments "Approved. {comment}"
  reject          The user decided the change is not wanted
                  needs --comment; on a closed issue only if closed as not planned; the user's decision: ask first, then --yes; labels -needs-review -changes-requested -blocked; comments "{comment}"; closes as not planned
  merged          The approved pull request has been merged into main
                  several numbers at once (merged 12 13 14) or a release's issues (release <tag> --verb merged); optional --comment; also on closed issues; refused with the label blocked; comments "{comment}"; closes as completed

Every verb adds the issue to the board if it is missing and refuses a
closed issue unless noted. A repeat is safe: an effect already in place
(status, comment, labels, assignees, blocked-by link, closed or open) is
skipped.

Lifecycle (from → to):
  start           Backlog → In progress
  hold            In progress, Changes requested → status unchanged
  resume          In progress, Changes requested, Approved → status unchanged
  review          In progress, Changes requested → In review
  request-changes In review → Changes requested
  approve         In review → Approved; asks the user first (--yes)
  reject          In progress, In review, Changes requested, Approved → status unchanged; closes as not planned, asks the user first (--yes)
  merged          Approved → Merged; closes as completed
  Initial:        Backlog (new issues; also an issue with no status or not on the board)
  Final:          Merged (gh dojo list hides it unless --all)
  Resolved:       Merged (a blocker in these no longer blocks)

Exit codes:
  0  everything applied: go on
  1  bad arguments or config: fix them as the error says
  2  a process check refused: don't work around it; ask the user
  3  issue or board not found: check the number (gh dojo list) or board.owner/project in .github/dojo.toml
  4  network, rate limit or auth: retry later, or gh auth refresh -s project
  5  partially applied: re-run the same command; it finishes the rest
  A verb on several issues (batch) exits 0 when all are done, 5 when some were
  written and a re-run may finish the rest, else with the code of the failed
  ones (2 first, then 1, 4, 3); a summary names each issue not done.
--- stderr
